findings.description:
The removed controller property was computed from `model.website`, so the header updated when the website changed. The template now reads the server-supplied `model.website_name`, but `User#save` only copies `bio_excerpt` back from the response (`app/assets/javascripts/discourse/models/user.js.es6:209-213`).

After editing the website in preferences:
- the link text shows the old name while `href={{model.website}}` points to the new URL;
- a newly added website does not appear at all until a full reload;
- a cleared website keeps showing.

Set `website_name` from `data.user.website_name` in the save callback; the `update` action already returns `UserSerializer` output.

The three new examples cover the equal-host branch and both outcomes of the `else` branch. Not covered:

- the `elsif` branch (`www.example.com` vs `forum.example.com`, line 144-146), which is the most complex one;
- a blank website, or an unparseable or scheme-less one (the `rescue nil` / `return` path);
- the restricted case: `untrusted_attributes` in the TL0-anonymous context (line 11) does not include `website_name`, and no TL0 example sets a website, so the leak above goes undetected.
